/Alt ()
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 765 0 R
/ActualText (through direct access to nonlocal variables \(declared elsewhere but visible in the sub- program\) or through parameter passing.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 766 0 R
/ActualText ( Data passed through parameters are accessed through names that are local to the subprogram. Parameter passing is more flexible than direct access to nonlocal variables. In essence, a subprogram with parameter access to the data that it is to process is a parameterized computation)
/Alt ()
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 767 0 R
/ActualText (.parameterized computation : It can perform its computation on whatever data it receivesthrough its parameters \(presuming the types of the parameters are as expectedby the subprogram\).)
/Alt ()
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 768 0 R
/ActualText ( If data access is through nonlocal variables, the only way the computation can proceed on different data is to assign new values to those nonlocal variables between calls to the subprogram. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
