492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 827 0 R
/ActualText (Parameter-passing methods are the ways in which parameters are transmitted to and/or from called subprograms)
/Alt ()
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Modes: IN: Passes info from caller to the callee. OUT: Callee writes values in the caller. IN/OUT: The caller tells the callee the value of the variable, which the callee may update.)
/E (Modes: IN: Passes info from caller to the callee. OUT: Callee writes values in the caller. IN/OUT: The caller tells the callee the value of the variable, which the callee may update.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Pass By Value)
/Alt ()
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 828 0 R
/ActualText (This method uses in-mode semantics. Changes made to formal parameters do not get transmitted back to the caller. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 829 0 R
/ActualText (Any modifications to the formal parameter variable inside the called function or method affect only the separate storage location and will not be reflected in the actual parameter in the calling environment. This method is also called call by value.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
