/Pg 39 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 830 0 R
/ActualText (When a parameter is passedby value, the value of the actual parameter is used to initialize the corresponding formal parameter, which then acts as a local variable in the subprogram, thus implementing in-mode semantics.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 831 0 R
/ActualText (Pass-by-value is normally implemented by copy, because accesses often are more efficient with this approach.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 832 0 R
/ActualText (Advantages:)
/Alt ()
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 833 0 R
/ActualText (Safety: Since a copy of the variable is passed, the original variable remains unchanged. This minimizes side effects, making code easier to understand and debug.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 834 0 R
/ActualText (Simplicity: It is often simpler to reason about functions that operate on copies of data. You can be confident that the function will not alter the state of the original argument.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 835 0 R
/ActualText (Concurrency: In multi-threaded environments, pass by value can be safer because each thread operates on its own copy of data, reducing the risk of race conditions.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 836 0 R
/ActualText (Use Pass by Value when you want to ensure that the original data remains unchanged and when working with small data types where copying is not costly.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Pass by Reference in C?)
/E (Pass by Reference in C?)
/Alt ()
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 837 0 R
/ActualText (In pass by reference, we pass the address of the variable instead of passing the value of the variable and access the variable using the pointers in the Function. All the changes made to variable in the function will be reflected in the main Program.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Example:)
/E (Example:)
/Alt ()
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
526 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 838 0 R
/ActualText (Consider Pass by reference as google drive and Call by value as bluetooth system. If you receive a file via bluetooth, any changes made to that file will only affect your file and not the main file, which is the core concept of call by reference, whereas any changes made to a file in Google Drive will be reflected everywhere, which is the main ideology behind pass by reference.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
